.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_match_limit \- set the match limit
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_set_match_limit(\fBpcre2_match_context\fP *\fImcontext\fP,
                          \fBuint32_t\fP \fIlimit\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function sets the match limit field in a match context. The result is
always zero.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.